RedCrow <drugo1979@levamisonounfiltroyahoo.it> wrote:
> Another thing i want to ask: is it normal that the Hello world program that
> i compiled on my linux box, doesn't run on the digital unix box with alpha?

Linux understands _too_ a format of executables used by DU and at least
an important subset of system calls.  Hence a program from DU has a
reasonable chance to work on Linux (there are various limitations).  The
other way around you will find "what you are talking about?" response
unless you are really cross-compiling.
  
> And more: can i compile a kernel on that unix box??

Here you are talking about something else.  By default an answer will
be "no".  Kernel is NOT written in Standard C in the first place
and is also special in many other aspects.  If you wonder if you can
set up a toolchain on DU to compile a kernel then the answer is
"certainly but it may not be that easy" and a question is why.

   Michal


