>> 
>> The I copy the kernel to /boot/ and booted it from aboot without problems.
> 
> Did you copy the initrd to /boot?

Well, he boots "without problems" and if this is really the case then
initrd is not doing anything useful or is required for anything
(assuming that "without problems" means also that all mount types are
correct).  OTOH we do not even know if various hardware support was
configured and, if this was attempted in form of modules, if these
modules are in place and even if a support for module loading was
turned on in this kernel.

For a known fixed configuration one can have most of anything as
built-in (some things are available only as modules - various
netfilter features, for example).

   Michal


